  {
   "text": "On the twenty-sixth of July 1920, the Boston Post started asking hard questions.",
   "start": 0.0,
   "end": 6.08
  },
  {
   "text": "Investors lost about twenty million dollars in nineteen-twenty money.",
   "start": 6.66,
   "end": 10.82
  },
  {
   "text": "Charged with eighty-six counts of mail fraud, Ponzi was sentenced to five years in federal prison.",
   "start": 11.62,
   "end": 17.08
  },
  {
   "text": "Released in 1934, he told reporters that he went looking for trouble and found it.",
   "start": 17.98,
   "end": 23.1
  },
  {
   "text": "He died in Rio de Janeiro in 1949, leaving an estate of seventy-five dollars.",
   "start": 23.52,
   "end": 29.287
  },
  {
   "text": "Would you have trusted a promise of fifty percent in forty-five days?",
